+++++++++++++++++++++ Requirements ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
+++++++ STEP 1 ++++++++++
1. Create database
Create a database named fintrack_db.
2. Create users table
id — primary key, auto-increment
name — user's name
email — unique
password — hashed password
created_at
updated_at
3. Connect Node.js to MySQL
Configure the backend so it can connect to fintrack_db.
4. Create database configuration
Keep database credentials in environment variables.
Do not hard-code the password in the source code.
5. Test the connection
Make sure the Node.js backend can successfully connect to MySQL.

+++++++ STEP 2 ++++++++++
1. Create Register API
POST /api/auth/register
2. Accept
name
email
password
3. Validate
All fields required.
Email must be valid.
Email must not already exist.
Password must meet a reasonable minimum length.
4. Hash password
Hash the password before storing it.
Never store the plain-text password.
5. Create user
Insert the user into the existing users table.
6. API response
Return success message and basic user information.
Do not return password_hash.
7. Handle errors
Duplicate email.
Invalid input.
Database/server errors.